    "rationale": "Chosen: NO_FIX. The violating path launches from the cycle_counter DFF (uart_rx.v:170) and ends in an async-FIFO write-pointer flop (wptr_full.v:52). 12 of 14 cells are unattributed, and the cell sequence (decode network cells 1-8, then XOR2/XOR2/XOR2/NOR3 in cells 9-12) is clearly binary-to-Gray conversion plus pointer-compare logic living in wptr_full.v, not in the shown counter. The only combinational logic in the given scope is `cycle_counter + 1'b1`, which feeds back into cycle_counter and is a different fan-out cone than the endpoint _125646_; it does not sit on this path. RETIME rejected: the sole register in scope (cycle_counter) is the startpoint, not a register inside the offending chain, and moving it would cross a module boundary and alter counter timing. RESTRUCTURE rejected: the deep chain is the Gray/compare network in wptr_full.v and unseen glue logic; rebalancing the counter increment cannot change the launch flop clk-to-Q (0.080 ns intrinsic) and does not touch this path. PIPELINE rejected: inserting a register on cycle_counter or its output delays the baud/bit-time count by a cycle (function change) and the reconvergent read-pointer compare that would need equal delay is outside this scope. A correct fix would retime or add a pipeline/synchronizer stage inside wptr_full.v's Gray-code compare / full-detect logic (with matching rebalance on the read-pointer side), which is not in the provided line range."
